                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apal.2012.01.011"}> doi:10.1016/j.apal.2012.01.011
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6272"} arXiv:1201.6272
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Palmgren"}> Erik Palmgren
                ,
                %em Bishop-style constructive mathematics in type theory – a tutorial
                (2013) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://staff.math.su.se/palmgren/Palmgren_Nis.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Palmgren-BishopConstructiveMathematics.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The term “Bishop set” and their formalization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            (essentially as for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/setoids"} setoids
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
          %ul
            %li#CoquandSpiwack
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"}> Thierry Coquand
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Spiwack"} Arnaud Spiwack
              = succeed "," do
                %em Towards constructive homological algebra in type theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Towards Mechanized Mathematical Assistants. MKM Calculemus 2007
              %strong 4573
              Springer (2007) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-73086-6_4"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-540-73086-6_4
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://hal.inria.fr/inria-00432525/document"} pdf
          %p Some of the text above is taken from this section.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+topos"} predicative topos
            formed by Bishop sets in type theory is discussed in
          %ul#vdBerg
            %li#MoerdijkPalmgren
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Palmgren"} Erik Palmgren
                %em Wellfounded trees in categories. Ann. Pure Appl. Logic, 104(1-3):189–218, (2000)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"}> Benno van den Berg
                ,
                %em Predicative toposes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0959"}> arXiv:1207.0959
                )
          %p
            A formalization of constructive set theory in terms of setoids in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            coded in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#PalmgrenWilander
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Palmgren"}> Erik Palmgren
              , Olov Wilander,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Constructing categories of setoids in type theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www2.math.su.se/~palmgren/coq/czf_and_setoids/czf&setoids.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www2.math.su.se/~palmgren/coq/czf_and_setoids"} Coq
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UF-IAS-2012"}> UF-IAS-2012
                ,
                %em On the setoid model of type theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://video.ias.edu/univalent/palmgren"}> video
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UF-IAS-2012"}> UF-IAS-2012
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://uf-ias-2012.wikispaces.com/Setoid+model+of+type+theory+formalized"} Setoid model of type theory formalized
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/10/syntax_semantics_and_structura.html#c029271"} Discussion
                on categorical aspects of the setoid construction.
